6: notes, compute which days already have entries for archive marking), and cover\n37: it with unit tests following the existing `src/lib/services/` + tests pattern.\n38: files: src/lib/services/JournalService.ts (new),\n39:        tests/unit/services/JournalService.test.ts (new)\n40: depends: TASK-1 (reads `is_system`)\n41: risk: medium — foundational logic the interface depends on; must be kept\n42: purely functional and well tested.\n43: \n44: TASK-3: Teach the Notes store about the journal — resolve the journal folder\n45: from the loaded categories, exclude journal entries/folder from ordinary\n46: surfaces (category tree, `getNewestNotes`/`getLastUpdatedNotes`/`getFavorites`,\n47: `getNotesForCategory(null)`), and add a method to open a journal day\n48: (resolve by title, create-on-first-open via `ApiService`, set `activeNote`).\n49: Extend the existing store unit tests for the new behavior.\n50: files: src/lib/state/Notes.svelte.ts, tests/unit/stores/Notes.test.ts\n51: depends: TASK-1, TASK-2\n52: risk: high — touches the shared `load()`/derived getters used by every\n53: notebook surface; an over-broad filter would hide ordinary notes.\n54: \n55: TASK-4: Add the journal i18n keys (Journal, Today, Yesterday, Other/archive,\n56: datepicker labels, empty-day text, create/error messages as needed) to the\n57: translation type and to all four locale tables (`en`, `de`, `es`, `fr`).\n58: files: src/lib/types/translation.ts, src/lib/i18n/en.ts, src/lib/i18n/de.ts,\n59:        src/lib/i18n/es.ts, src/lib/i18n/fr.ts\n60: depends: none\n61: risk: low — mechanical, but `npm run check` fails if the four tables drift.\n62: \n63: TASK-5: Add the Journal navigation entry beside Favorites in both the desktop\n64: sidebar (`NoteNavigationDesktop.svelte`) and the mobile notebook drawer\n65: (`NoteNavigationMobile.svelte`), linking to the new journal route and never\n66: rendered as an expandable folder. Add the route to `urls.ts` if a\n67: date-addressed route is used.\n68: files: src/lib/components/notes/NoteNavigationDesktop.svelte,\n69:        src/lib/components/notes/NoteNavigationMobile.svelte,\n70:        src/lib/config/urls.ts\n71: depends: TASK-3, TASK-4\n72: risk: medium — two separate navigation variants; the mobile drawer level-1\n73: list currently also enumerates categories/no-category notes that must not\n74: include the journal.\n75: \n76: TASK-6: Build the Journal interface — a route/component presenting Today,\n77: Yesterday and Other (an archive datepicker), resolving the selected day's\n78: entry through the store, creating it on first open and handing it to the\n79: existing note editor (no note list). Restrict reach to today and earlier,\n80: mark days that already have entries, and disable future days. Reuse the\n81: existing `DatePicker` wrapper, extending it only if the pinned\n82: `@svelte-plugins/datepicker` cannot mark/disable days through the current\n83: wrapper.\n84: files: src/routes/notes/journal/** (new), src/lib/components/notes/journal/**\n85:        (new), src/lib/components/forms/DatePicker.svelte (only if extension\n86:        needed)\n87: depends: TASK-2, TASK-3, TASK-4\n88: risk: high — the main new surface; interacts with loading/active-note state\n89: and the editor, and the datepicker capability for marks/disabled days is not\n90: confirmed in this repo.\n91: \n92: TASK-7: Verification — run `npm run check`, `npm run lint` and `npm test` and\n93: resolve any fallout.\n94: depends: TASK-1 through TASK-6\n95: risk: low — standard verification gate.\n96: \n97: ## Open questions / scope notes\n98: \n99: - The brief wires the hidden-toggle endpoint \"so the client can … toggle\n100:   hidden\" and says \"only the journal uses it in this job\", but no journal UI\n101:   for toggling hidden is described (the API already provisions the folder\n102:   hidden). TASK-1 wires the endpoint; no UI task consumes it. If a\n103:   user-facing toggle is actually expected, that scope should be added\n104:   explicitly rather than assumed.\n105: - Route shape (`/notes/journal` vs a date-addressed `/notes/journal/date/[date]`\n106:   like `check-in/date/[date]`) is left to the developer; the brief calls this a\n107:   developer choice. TASK-5/TASK-6 assume a single journal route but do not fix\n108:   the path.\n109: - The `@svelte-plugins/datepicker` (v1.0.11) capability to mark days with\n110:   entries and disable future days is not verifiable from this worktree\n111:   (`node_modules` not present); if unsupported, the archive picker may need a\n112:   small extension or an alternative. Flagged under TASK-6.\n\n(End of file - total 112 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Tasks: notebook journal\n\nid: exist\nanalyst: analyst\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Summary\n\nBuild the notebook Journal surface on top of the API contract the brief\ndescribes: mirror the type/route contract, extract the pure day/entry\nresolution into a tested service, teach the Notes store about the system\njournal folder (and exclude it from ordinary notebook surfaces), add the\nJournal navigation entry, and build the day-based journal interface with an\narchive datepicker. i18n across all four locales and unit tests are part of\nthe work.\n\nBranch check: brief declares `branch: feature/exist_notebook-journal`. The\nworktree is mounted on the job branch (this session has no shell to run","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/exist_notebook-journal/tasks.md","text":"# Tasks: notebook journal\n\nid: exist\nanalyst: analyst\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Summary\n\nBuild the notebook Journal surface on top of the API contract the brief\ndescribes: mirror the type/route contract, extract the pure day/entry\nresolution into a tested service, teach the Notes store about the system\njournal folder (and exclude it from ordinary notebook surfaces), add the\nJournal navigation entry, and build the day-based journal interface with an\narchive datepicker. i18n across all four locales and unit tests are part of\nthe work.\n\nBranch check: brief declares `branch: feature/exist_notebook-journal`. The\nworktree is mounted on the job branch (this session has no shell to run\n`git branch --show-current`, so the check could not be repeated independently;\nthe workspace is a job worktree, which is on the job branch by construction).\n\n## Task breakdown\n\nTASK-1: Mirror the new API contract — add the `is_system`/`is_hidden` flags to\nthe `NoteCategory` type and wire the `PATCH /notes/categories/{id}/hidden`\nendpoint into `apiRoutes.notes`.\nfiles: src/lib/types/note.ts, src/lib/config/apiRoutes.ts\ndepends: none\nrisk: low — additive type fields plus one route constant, no behavior change.\n\nTASK-2: Extract the pure day/entry-resolution logic into a new\n`JournalService` (locate the journal folder by `is_system`, build the\n`YYYY-MM-DD` entry title via `getUrlFormat`, find an existing entry among\nnotes, compute which days already have entries for archive marking), and cover\nit with unit tests following the existing `src/lib/services/` + tests pattern.\nfiles: src/lib/services/JournalService.ts (new),\n       tests/unit/services/JournalService.test.ts (new)\ndepends: TASK-1 (reads `is_system`)\nrisk: medium — foundational logic the interface depends on; must be kept\npurely functional and well tested.\n\nTASK-3: Teach the Notes store about the journal — resolve the journal folder\nfrom the loaded categories, exclude journal entries/folder from ordinary\nsurfaces (category tree, `getNewestNotes`/`getLastUpdatedNotes`/`getFavorites`,\n`getNotesForCategory(null)`), and add a method to open a journal day\n(resolve by title, create-on-first-open via `ApiService`, set `activeNote`).\nExtend the existing store unit tests for the new behavior.\nfiles: src/lib/state/Notes.svelte.ts, tests/unit/stores/Notes.test.ts\ndepends: TASK-1, TASK-2\nrisk: high — touches the shared `load()`/derived getters used by every\nnotebook surface; an over-broad filter would hide ordinary notes.\n\nTASK-4: Add the journal i18n keys (Journal, Today, Yesterday, Other/archive,\ndatepicker labels, empty-day text, create/error messages as needed) to the\ntranslation type and to all four locale tables (`en`, `de`, `es`, `fr`).\nfiles: src/lib/types/translation.ts, src/lib/i18n/en.ts, src/lib/i18n/de.ts,\n       src/lib/i18n/es.ts, src/lib/i18n/fr.ts\ndepends: none\nrisk: low — mechanical, but `npm run check` fails if the four tables drift.\n\nTASK-5: Add the Journal navigation entry beside Favorites in both the desktop\nsidebar (`NoteNavigationDesktop.svelte`) and the mobile notebook drawer\n(`NoteNavigationMobile.svelte`), linking to the new journal route and never\nrendered as an expandable folder. Add the route to `urls.ts` if a\ndate-addressed route is used.\nfiles: src/lib/components/notes/NoteNavigationDesktop.svelte,\n       src/lib/components/notes/NoteNavigationMobile.svelte,\n       src/lib/config/urls.ts\ndepends: TASK-3, TASK-4\nrisk: medium — two separate navigation variants; the mobile drawer level-1\nlist currently also enumerates categories/no-category notes that must not\ninclude the journal.\n\nTASK-6: Build the Journal interface — a route/component presenting Today,\nYesterday and Other (an archive datepicker), resolving the selected day's\nentry through the store, creating it on first open and handing it to the\nexisting note editor (no note list). Restrict reach to today and earlier,\nmark days that already have entries, and disable future days. Reuse the\nexisting `DatePicker` wrapper, extending it only if the pinned\n`@svelte-plugins/datepicker` cannot mark/disable days through the current\nwrapper.\nfiles: src/routes/notes/journal/** (new), src/lib/components/notes/journal/**\n       (new), src/lib/components/forms/DatePicker.svelte (only if extension\n       needed)\ndepends: TASK-2, TASK-3, TASK-4\nrisk: high — the main new surface; interacts with loading/active-note state\nand the editor, and the datepicker capability for marks/disabled days is not\nconfirmed in this repo.\n\nTASK-7: Verification — run `npm run check`, `npm run lint` and `npm test` and\nresolve any fallout.\ndepends: TASK-1 through TASK-6\nrisk: low — standard verification gate.\n\n## Open questions / scope notes\n\n- The brief wires the hidden-toggle endpoint \"so the client can … toggle\n  hidden\" and says \"only the journal uses it in this job\", but no journal UI\n  for toggling hidden is described (the API already provisions the folder\n  hidden). TASK-1 wires the endpoint; no UI task consumes it. If a\n  user-facing toggle is actually expected, that scope should be added\n  explicitly rather than assumed.\n- Route shape (`/notes/journal` vs a date-addressed `/notes/journal/date/[date]`\n  like `check-in/date/[date]`) is left to the developer; the brief calls this a\n  developer choice. TASK-5/TASK-6 assume a single journal route but do not fix\n  the path.\n- The `@svelte-plugins/datepicker` (v1.0.11) capability to mark days with\n  entries and disable future days is not verifiable from this worktree\n  (`node_modules` not present); if unsupported, the archive picker may need a\n  small extension or an alternative. Flagged under TASK-6.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":112,"totalLines":112,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/exist_notebook-journal/tasks.md","time":{"start":1791639344973,"end":1791639345084}},"id":"prt_12606d6e3001Xq3giIj8ncFyk1","sessionID":"ses_ed9f94635ffee3zYlqCKAoMoF3","messageID":"msg_12606cf97001TzjEAMc5iD8I7K"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791639345116,"sessionID":"ses_ed9f94635ffee3zYlqCKAoMoF3","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01_L4jVLELw5Jsz7id0r3wG8175","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/exist_notebook-journal/implementation.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/exist_notebook-journal/implementation.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Implementation: notebook journal\n2: \n3: id: exist\n4: developer: opencode (deepseek-v4-flash)\n5: date: 2026-10-10\n6: \n7: <!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n8: \n9: ## Summary\n10: \n11: Built the notebook Journal surface on top of the API contract from the brief:\n12: \n13: - Mirrored the new contract (`is_system`/`is_hidden` on `NoteCategory`, the\n14:   hidden-toggle route).\n15: - Extracted the pure day/entry resolution into a new tested `JournalService`.\n16: - Taught the `Notes` store about the system journal folder: it is resolved from\n17:   the loaded categories, held separately, and excluded from every ordinary\n18:   notebook surface.\n19: - Added a **Journal** entry to the desktop sidebar and the mobile notebook\n20:   drawer, beside Favorites.\n21: - Added a day-based journal interface (Today / Yesterday / Other) at\n22:   `/notes/journal` that resolves the day's entry by the `YYYY-MM-DD` title\n23:   convention, creates it on first open, and hands it to the existing note\n24:   editor. The archive picker marks days that already have an entry and disables\n25:   future days.\n26: - Added the journal strings to all four locales and unit tests for the new\n27:   service and store behaviour.\n28: \n29: ## Changes\n30: \n31: TASK-1 — API contract:\n32: - `src/lib/types/note.ts`: added required `is_system` / `is_hidden` to\n33:   `NoteCategory`.\n34: - `src/lib/config/apiRoutes.ts`: added\n35:   `notes.updateCategoryHidden` (`PATCH /notes/categories/%d/hidden`).\n36: - `tests/unit/stores/Notes.test.ts`: the `category()` factory now provides the\n37:   two new required flags (type fallout only).\n38: \n39: TASK-2 — pure logic:\n40: - `src/lib/services/JournalService.ts` (new): `findJournalCategory` (by the\n41:   `is_system` flag, root or child), `getEntryTitle` (via `getUrlFormat`),\n42:   `isEntryTitle`, `findEntry`, `getEntryDates` and `isReachable` (day-granularity\n43:   today-and-earlier check).\n44: - `tests/unit/services/JournalService.test.ts` (new): 17 unit tests.\n45: \n46: TASK-3 — Notes store:\n47: - `src/lib/state/Notes.svelte.ts`: added `journalCategory` state and\n48:   `journalService`; `loadCategories()` now splits the system folder out of the\n49:   rendered tree; `getVisibleNotes()`/`getNotesForCategory`/`getNewestNotes`/\n50:   `getLastUpdatedNotes`/`getFavorites` exclude journal notes; added\n51:   `isJournalNote`, `getJournalEntry`, `getJournalEntryDates` and\n52:   `openJournalEntry` (resolve-or-create then set `activeNote`).\n53: - `src/routes/notes/+page.svelte`: the notebook-overview empty state now uses\n54:   visible notes so a journal-only notebook does not render a blank overview.\n55: - `tests/unit/stores/Notes.test.ts`: 8 new tests covering resolution,\n56:   create-on-first-open, the error/no-folder paths and the exclusions.\n57: \n58: TASK-4 — i18n:\n59: - `src/lib/types/translation.ts` + `en/de/es/fr`: added `journal`, `today`,\n60:   `yesterday`, `other`, `journal_empty`, `journal_create_error`.\n61: \n62: TASK-5 — navigation:\n63: - `src/lib/config/urls.ts`: added `urls.journal = '/notes/journal'`.\n64: - `NoteNavigationDesktop.svelte` / `NoteNavigationMobile.svelte`: added a\n65:   Journal destination beside Favorites as a plain link (never an expandable\n66:   folder); the mobile root list and the desktop no-category/empty checks now use\n67:   the journal-aware getters.\n68: \n69: TASK-6 — interface:\n70: - `src/routes/notes/journal/+page.svelte` (new): Today / Yesterday / Other\n71:   buttons; opens the selected day through the store; renders the existing\n72:   `TipTapEditor`; waits for notes + categories to load before resolving today.\n73: - `src/lib/components/notes/journal/JournalHeader.svelte` (new): date-aware\n74:   heading (Today/Yesterday/formatted date) plus Save.\n75: - `src/lib/components/notes/journal/JournalArchivePicker.svelte` (new): month\n76:   grid built on the existing `getCalendarMonth` helper; marks days with an entry\n77:   and disables future days; cannot advance past the current month.\n78: - `src/lib/components/notes/editor/TipTapEditor.svelte`: added an optional\n79:   `autofocus` prop so Today opens write-ready while past days open read-first.\n80: \n81: TASK-7 — verification: see below.\n82: \n83: ## Known issues / follow-ups\n84: \n85: - **Archive picker is a custom component, not the `DatePicker` wrapper.** The\n86:   pinned `@svelte-plugins/datepicker` (1.0.11) can disable future days\n87:   (`enableFutureDates`) but has no way to mark days that already have an entry —\n88:   it only exposes `enabledDates`/`disabledDates`, and day cells are rendered by\n89:   the library with no per-date hook. The task list explicitly allowed \"a small\n90:   extension or an alternative\"; the archive picker is therefore a small custom\n91:   month grid built on the repo's existing `getCalendarMonth` helper, giving full\n92:   control over marking and disabled days. `DatePicker.svelte` was left untouched.\n93: - **`npm run lint` fails on the branch before this change** (pre-existing):\n94:   `prettier --check` flags ~252 files and `eslint` reports ~292 errors\n95:   (`svelte/no-navigation-without-resolve`, unused imports, ...). Every file\n96:   changed here except the new ones was already on that list; the added lines are\n97:   prettier- and eslint-clean. `npm run format` was deliberately not run\n98:   repo-wide (it would reformat hundreds of unrelated files). The one eslint error\n99:   in a touched file (`NoteNavigationMobile.svelte`, unused `fade` import) is\n100:   pre-existing and left untouched.\n101: - **`npm test` has one pre-existing failure** unrelated to this job:\n102:   `tests/components/logic-leaves.test.ts > StatisticWidget > applies the\n103:   requested color classes`. All other 748 tests pass (25 of which are new here).\n104: - **No rendered/visual verification.** The app is a client-only SPA behind auth\n105:   and has no local backend in this worktree, so `shot` would only capture the\n106:   login redirect. Verification was done with `npm run check` (0 errors / 0\n107:   warnings), `npm run build` (succeeds, journal route emitted) and `npm test`.\n108: - The hidden-toggle route is wired (TASK-1) but unused, per the analyst's note\n109:   that no journal UI consumes it in this job.\n\n(End of file - total 109 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Implementation: notebook journal\n\nid: exist\ndeveloper: opencode (deepseek-v4-flash)\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n\n## Summary\n\nBuilt the notebook Journal surface on top of the API contract from the brief:\n\n- Mirrored the new contract (`is_system`/`is_hidden` on `NoteCategory`, the\n  hidden-toggle route).\n- Extracted the pure day/entry resolution into a new tested `JournalService`.\n- Taught the `Notes` store about the system journal folder: it is resolved from\n  the loaded categories, held separately, and excluded from every ordinary\n  notebook surface.\n- Added a **Journal** entry to the desktop sidebar and the mobile notebook\n  drawer, beside Favorites.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/exist_notebook-journal/implementation.md","text":"# Implementation: notebook journal\n\nid: exist\ndeveloper: opencode (deepseek-v4-flash)\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n\n## Summary\n\nBuilt the notebook Journal surface on top of the API contract from the brief:\n\n- Mirrored the new contract (`is_system`/`is_hidden` on `NoteCategory`, the\n  hidden-toggle route).\n- Extracted the pure day/entry resolution into a new tested `JournalService`.\n- Taught the `Notes` store about the system journal folder: it is resolved from\n  the loaded categories, held separately, and excluded from every ordinary\n  notebook surface.\n- Added a **Journal** entry to the desktop sidebar and the mobile notebook\n  drawer, beside Favorites.\n- Added a day-based journal interface (Today / Yesterday / Other) at\n  `/notes/journal` that resolves the day's entry by the `YYYY-MM-DD` title\n  convention, creates it on first open, and hands it to the existing note\n  editor. The archive picker marks days that already have an entry and disables\n  future days.\n- Added the journal strings to all four locales and unit tests for the new\n  service and store behaviour.\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1 — API contract:\n- `src/lib/types/note.ts`: added required `is_system` / `is_hidden` to\n  `NoteCategory`.\n- `src/lib/config/apiRoutes.ts`: added\n  `notes.updateCategoryHidden` (`PATCH /notes/categories/%d/hidden`).\n- `tests/unit/stores/Notes.test.ts`: the `category()` factory now provides the\n  two new required flags (type fallout only).\n\nTASK-2 — pure logic:\n- `src/lib/services/JournalService.ts` (new): `findJournalCategory` (by the\n  `is_system` flag, root or child), `getEntryTitle` (via `getUrlFormat`),\n  `isEntryTitle`, `findEntry`, `getEntryDates` and `isReachable` (day-granularity\n  today-and-earlier check).\n- `tests/unit/services/JournalService.test.ts` (new): 17 unit tests.\n\nTASK-3 — Notes store:\n- `src/lib/state/Notes.svelte.ts`: added `journalCategory` state and\n  `journalService`; `loadCategories()` now splits the system folder out of the\n  rendered tree; `getVisibleNotes()`/`getNotesForCategory`/`getNewestNotes`/\n  `getLastUpdatedNotes`/`getFavorites` exclude journal notes; added\n  `isJournalNote`, `getJournalEntry`, `getJournalEntryDates` and\n  `openJournalEntry` (resolve-or-create then set `activeNote`).\n- `src/routes/notes/+page.svelte`: the notebook-overview empty state now uses\n  visible notes so a journal-only notebook does not render a blank overview.\n- `tests/unit/stores/Notes.test.ts`: 8 new tests covering resolution,\n  create-on-first-open, the error/no-folder paths and the exclusions.\n\nTASK-4 — i18n:\n- `src/lib/types/translation.ts` + `en/de/es/fr`: added `journal`, `today`,\n  `yesterday`, `other`, `journal_empty`, `journal_create_error`.\n\nTASK-5 — navigation:\n- `src/lib/config/urls.ts`: added `urls.journal = '/notes/journal'`.\n- `NoteNavigationDesktop.svelte` / `NoteNavigationMobile.svelte`: added a\n  Journal destination beside Favorites as a plain link (never an expandable\n  folder); the mobile root list and the desktop no-category/empty checks now use\n  the journal-aware getters.\n\nTASK-6 — interface:\n- `src/routes/notes/journal/+page.svelte` (new): Today / Yesterday / Other\n  buttons; opens the selected day through the store; renders the existing\n  `TipTapEditor`; waits for notes + categories to load before resolving today.\n- `src/lib/components/notes/journal/JournalHeader.svelte` (new): date-aware\n  heading (Today/Yesterday/formatted date) plus Save.\n- `src/lib/components/notes/journal/JournalArchivePicker.svelte` (new): month\n  grid built on the existing `getCalendarMonth` helper; marks days with an entry\n  and disables future days; cannot advance past the current month.\n- `src/lib/components/notes/editor/TipTapEditor.svelte`: added an optional\n  `autofocus` prop so Today opens write-ready while past days open read-first.\n\nTASK-7 — verification: see below.\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- **Archive picker is a custom component, not the `DatePicker` wrapper.** The\n  pinned `@svelte-plugins/datepicker` (1.0.11) can disable future days\n  (`enableFutureDates`) but has no way to mark days that already have an entry —\n  it only exposes `enabledDates`/`disabledDates`, and day cells are rendered by\n  the library with no per-date hook. The task list explicitly allowed \"a small\n  extension or an alternative\"; the archive picker is therefore a small custom\n  month grid built on the repo's existing `getCalendarMonth` helper, giving full\n  control over marking and disabled days. `DatePicker.svelte` was left untouched.\n- **`npm run lint` fails on the branch before this change** (pre-existing):\n  `prettier --check` flags ~252 files and `eslint` reports ~292 errors\n  (`svelte/no-navigation-without-resolve`, unused imports, ...). Every file\n  changed here except the new ones was already on that list; the added lines are\n  prettier- and eslint-clean. `npm run format` was deliberately not run\n  repo-wide (it would reformat hundreds of unrelated files). The one eslint error\n  in a touched file (`NoteNavigationMobile.svelte`, unused `fade` import) is\n  pre-existing and left untouched.\n- **`npm test` has one pre-existing failure** unrelated to this job:\n  `tests/components/logic-leaves.test.ts > StatisticWidget > applies the\n  requested color classes`. All other 748 tests pass (25 of which are new here).\n- **No rendered/visual verification.** The app is a client-only SPA behind auth\n  and has no local backend in this worktree, so `shot` would only capture the\n  login redirect. Verification was done with `npm run check` (0 errors / 0\n  warnings), `npm run build` (succeeds, journal route emitted) and `npm test`.\n- The hidden-toggle route is wired (TASK-1) but unused, per the analyst's note\n  that no journal UI consumes it in this job.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":109,"totalLines":109,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/exist_notebook-journal/implementation.md","time":{"start":1791639345045,"end":1791639345103}},"id":"prt_12606d751001CAEBSdPz6FI5Mb","sessionID":"ses_ed9f94635ffee3zYlqCKAoMoF3","messageID":"msg_12606cf97001TzjEAMc5iD8I7K"}}
