{"type":"text","timestamp":1791639451779,"sessionID":"ses_ed9f94635ffee3zYlqCKAoMoF3","part":{"id":"prt_126087242001kKTgkFflzoozW7","messageID":"msg_126086b6f0011Thpd2YGFGg4XP","sessionID":"ses_ed9f94635ffee3zYlqCKAoMoF3","type":"text","text":"I completed the review and committed `verdict.md`.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Verdict: NEEDS WORK** — one blocker.\n\nI verified the branch (`feature/exist_notebook-journal`), read `brief.md`/`tasks.md`/`implementation.md`, and reviewed the full diff against `main` (`git diff main...HEAD`).\n\nPer task:\n- **TASK-1 PASS** — `is_system`/`is_hidden` on `NoteCategory` + `updateCategoryHidden` route.\n- **TASK-2 PASS** — pure `JournalService` + 17 tests (note: `isReachable` is only used by tests, non-blocking).\n- **TASK-3 PARTIAL** — the store getters filter the journal correctly, but the notebook overview doesn't reliably.\n- **TASK-4 PASS** — all six keys in all four locales.\n- **TASK-5 PASS** — Journal link in desktop + mobile nav beside Favorites.\n- **TASK-6 PASS** — day-based `/notes/journal` route, create-on-first-open, archive picker marking/disabled-future-days.\n- **TASK-7 PASS** — reported checks/build/tests; one pre-existing unrelated test failure and pre-existing lint noise.\n\n**The blocker (TASK-3):** `src/routes/notes/+layout.svelte:73` loads notes and categories concurrently (`Promise.all`). `load()` (`Notes.svelte.ts:64-66`) snapshots `newestNotes`/`lastUpdatedNotes`/`favoriteNotes` using getters that only filter when `journalCategory` is already resolved. `src/routes/notes/+page.svelte:12-14` renders from those snapshot fields. If `GET /notes` lands before `GET /notes/categories`, journal entries leak into the notebook overview's newest/favorites/last-updated — a direct violation of the brief. Fix: derive the overview from the live getters (as the nav components already do) or re-snapshot the fields after `loadCategories()`.\n\nNo scope creep or unrelated refactors; no security findings. The verdict commit is in place: `26e59dc [exist] verdict: NEEDS WORK — fix journal leak into notebook overview under concurrent load`.","time":{"start":1791639450178,"end":1791639451774}}}
