{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791639639340,"sessionID":"ses_ed9f4e243ffefIDWX0046IKymc","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_WDbQrD0e0eOKhMEnnNs07527","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/exist_notebook-journal/verdict.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/exist_notebook-journal/verdict.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Verdict: notebook journal\n2: \n3: id: exist\n4: reviewer: reviewer (deepseek-v4-flash)\n5: date: 2026-10-10\n6: \n7: <!-- Produced by @reviewer and/or @security after implementation. -->\n8: \n9: ## Review\n10: \n11: TASK-1: PASS\n12: notes: `is_system`/`is_hidden` added to `NoteCategory` (`src/lib/types/note.ts`) and\n13: `updateCategoryHidden` wired in `src/lib/config/apiRoutes.ts`. The test factory in\n14: `tests/unit/stores/Notes.test.ts` was updated for the new required fields. Contract\n15: mirrors the brief.\n16: \n17: TASK-2: PASS\n18: notes: `JournalService` (`src/lib/services/JournalService.ts`) is pure; resolution is by\n19: `is_system` (not title), entry titles use `getUrlFormat`, archive dates and\n20: day-granularity reachability are covered. 17 tests in\n21: `tests/unit/services/JournalService.test.ts`.\n22: Non-blocking: `isReachable` is not used in production code (the archive picker\n23: re-implements the future check as `isFuture`); it is only exercised by tests. The\n24: requirement is still met, so this does not block.\n25: \n26: TASK-3: PARTIAL\n27: notes: The store resolves the journal folder and excludes it from the nav getters\n28: (`getNotesForCategory`/`getVisibleNotes`/`getNewestNotes`/`getLastUpdatedNotes`/\n29: `getFavorites`) correctly, and the new tests pass. But the notebook overview does not\n30: reliably use those filters:\n31: - `src/routes/notes/+layout.svelte:73` loads categories and notes concurrently:\n32:   `await Promise.all([notes.loadCategories(), notes.load(), tags.load()])`.\n33: - `src/lib/state/Notes.svelte.ts:64-66` — `load()` snapshots\n34:   `newestNotes`/`lastUpdatedNotes`/`favoriteNotes` from the getters, which only filter\n35:   when `journalCategory` is already set (set by `loadCategories()` at line 95).\n36: - `src/routes/notes/+page.svelte:12-14` renders the notebook overview from those\n37:   snapshot fields.\n38: So when `GET /notes` resolves before `GET /notes/categories`, `journalCategory` is still\n39: `null`, `isJournalNote()` returns false, and journal entries leak into the overview's\n40: newest / favorites / last-updated lists — a direct violation of the brief's\n41: \"Journal entries must not appear in … the notebook overview (newest / favorites /\n42: last-updated)\". The new store tests do not catch this because they set\n43: `journalCategory` directly before exercising the getters.\n44: Suggested fix: render the overview from the live getters (as the navigation components\n45: already do with `getFavorites()`), or re-snapshot the three fields at the end of\n46: `loadCategories()`.\n47: \n48: TASK-4: PASS\n49: notes: All six keys (`journal`, `today`, `yesterday`, `other`, `journal_empty`,\n50: `journal_create_error`) added to `NoteRecords` and to `en/de/es/fr`. No drift.\n51: \n52: TASK-5: PASS\n53: notes: Journal link added to `NoteNavigationDesktop.svelte` and\n54: `NoteNavigationMobile.svelte` beside Favorites as a plain link; `urls.journal` added.\n55: Mobile root list uses the journal-aware getter and the folder is filtered out of\n56: `categories`. `resolve(urls.journal)` matches the existing static-route pattern.\n57: \n58: TASK-6: PASS\n59: notes: `/notes/journal` (`src/routes/notes/journal/+page.svelte`) with Today / Yesterday /\n60: Other, resolved through `openJournalEntry` (create-on-first-open) into the existing\n61: `TipTapEditor`. The custom `JournalArchivePicker` marks days with entries and disables\n62: future days (YYYY-MM-DD lexicographic compare) and never advances past the current\n63: month; the task allowed an alternative to the `DatePicker` wrapper. `autofocus={isToday}`\n64: gives today write-ready / past days read-first. No note list. The picker's weekday\n65: headers (1–7, Monday-first) line up with `getCalendarMonth`.\n66: \n67: TASK-7: PASS\n68: notes: Developer reports `npm run check` (0/0), `npm run build` (route emitted) and\n69: `npm test` (748 pass, 1 pre-existing unrelated failure). The lint failure is documented\n70: as pre-existing (repo-wide prettier/eslint) and not caused by this change. I could not\n71: re-run these in this session (shell is restricted to git), so this relies on the\n72: reported results plus reading. No new verification gap beyond the TASK-3 issue.\n73: \n74: Scope: no unrelated refactors. All changed files map to the tasks. `TipTapEditor`\n75: autofocus, the notes overview empty-state checks, and the nav getter swaps are all in\n76: scope.\n77: \n78: ## Security\n79: \n80: none — no auth, secret, or data-flow changes; new endpoint constant is consistent with\n81: the existing route table.\n82: \n83: ## Overall\n84: \n85: NEEDS WORK\n86: \n87: Must change before merge:\n88: 1. Make journal exclusion robust under the concurrent `load()`/`loadCategories()` calls\n89:    (TASK-3). The notebook overview at `src/routes/notes/+page.svelte` reads the snapshot\n90:    fields `notes.favoriteNotes`/`notes.newestNotes`/`notes.lastUpdatedNotes`, which are\n91:    populated by `load()` before `journalCategory` may be resolved. Either derive the\n92:    overview from the live getters or re-snapshot those fields at the end of\n93:    `loadCategories()`. A store test that runs `load()` and `loadCategories()`\n94:    concurrently (or asserts the fields are filtered once `journalCategory` is set) would\n95:    lock this down.\n\n(End of file - total 95 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Verdict: notebook journal\n\nid: exist\nreviewer: reviewer (deepseek-v4-flash)\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n<!-- Produced by @reviewer and/or @security after implementation. -->\n\n## Review\n\nTASK-1: PASS\nnotes: `is_system`/`is_hidden` added to `NoteCategory` (`src/lib/types/note.ts`) and\n`updateCategoryHidden` wired in `src/lib/config/apiRoutes.ts`. The test factory in\n`tests/unit/stores/Notes.test.ts` was updated for the new required fields. Contract\nmirrors the brief.\n\nTASK-2: PASS\nnotes: `JournalService` (`src/lib/services/JournalService.ts`) is pure; resolution is by\n`is_system` (not title), entry titles use `getUrlFormat`, archive dates and\nday-granularity reachability are covered. 17 tests in","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/exist_notebook-journal/verdict.md","text":"# Verdict: notebook journal\n\nid: exist\nreviewer: reviewer (deepseek-v4-flash)\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n<!-- Produced by @reviewer and/or @security after implementation. -->\n\n## Review\n\nTASK-1: PASS\nnotes: `is_system`/`is_hidden` added to `NoteCategory` (`src/lib/types/note.ts`) and\n`updateCategoryHidden` wired in `src/lib/config/apiRoutes.ts`. The test factory in\n`tests/unit/stores/Notes.test.ts` was updated for the new required fields. Contract\nmirrors the brief.\n\nTASK-2: PASS\nnotes: `JournalService` (`src/lib/services/JournalService.ts`) is pure; resolution is by\n`is_system` (not title), entry titles use `getUrlFormat`, archive dates and\nday-granularity reachability are covered. 17 tests in\n`tests/unit/services/JournalService.test.ts`.\nNon-blocking: `isReachable` is not used in production code (the archive picker\nre-implements the future check as `isFuture`); it is only exercised by tests. The\nrequirement is still met, so this does not block.\n\nTASK-3: PARTIAL\nnotes: The store resolves the journal folder and excludes it from the nav getters\n(`getNotesForCategory`/`getVisibleNotes`/`getNewestNotes`/`getLastUpdatedNotes`/\n`getFavorites`) correctly, and the new tests pass. But the notebook overview does not\nreliably use those filters:\n- `src/routes/notes/+layout.svelte:73` loads categories and notes concurrently:\n  `await Promise.all([notes.loadCategories(), notes.load(), tags.load()])`.\n- `src/lib/state/Notes.svelte.ts:64-66` — `load()` snapshots\n  `newestNotes`/`lastUpdatedNotes`/`favoriteNotes` from the getters, which only filter\n  when `journalCategory` is already set (set by `loadCategories()` at line 95).\n- `src/routes/notes/+page.svelte:12-14` renders the notebook overview from those\n  snapshot fields.\nSo when `GET /notes` resolves before `GET /notes/categories`, `journalCategory` is still\n`null`, `isJournalNote()` returns false, and journal entries leak into the overview's\nnewest / favorites / last-updated lists — a direct violation of the brief's\n\"Journal entries must not appear in … the notebook overview (newest / favorites /\nlast-updated)\". The new store tests do not catch this because they set\n`journalCategory` directly before exercising the getters.\nSuggested fix: render the overview from the live getters (as the navigation components\nalready do with `getFavorites()`), or re-snapshot the three fields at the end of\n`loadCategories()`.\n\nTASK-4: PASS\nnotes: All six keys (`journal`, `today`, `yesterday`, `other`, `journal_empty`,\n`journal_create_error`) added to `NoteRecords` and to `en/de/es/fr`. No drift.\n\nTASK-5: PASS\nnotes: Journal link added to `NoteNavigationDesktop.svelte` and\n`NoteNavigationMobile.svelte` beside Favorites as a plain link; `urls.journal` added.\nMobile root list uses the journal-aware getter and the folder is filtered out of\n`categories`. `resolve(urls.journal)` matches the existing static-route pattern.\n\nTASK-6: PASS\nnotes: `/notes/journal` (`src/routes/notes/journal/+page.svelte`) with Today / Yesterday /\nOther, resolved through `openJournalEntry` (create-on-first-open) into the existing\n`TipTapEditor`. The custom `JournalArchivePicker` marks days with entries and disables\nfuture days (YYYY-MM-DD lexicographic compare) and never advances past the current\nmonth; the task allowed an alternative to the `DatePicker` wrapper. `autofocus={isToday}`\ngives today write-ready / past days read-first. No note list. The picker's weekday\nheaders (1–7, Monday-first) line up with `getCalendarMonth`.\n\nTASK-7: PASS\nnotes: Developer reports `npm run check` (0/0), `npm run build` (route emitted) and\n`npm test` (748 pass, 1 pre-existing unrelated failure). The lint failure is documented\nas pre-existing (repo-wide prettier/eslint) and not caused by this change. I could not\nre-run these in this session (shell is restricted to git), so this relies on the\nreported results plus reading. No new verification gap beyond the TASK-3 issue.\n\nScope: no unrelated refactors. All changed files map to the tasks. `TipTapEditor`\nautofocus, the notes overview empty-state checks, and the nav getter swaps are all in\nscope.\n\n## Security\n\nnone — no auth, secret, or data-flow changes; new endpoint constant is consistent with\nthe existing route table.\n\n## Overall\n\nNEEDS WORK\n\nMust change before merge:\n1. Make journal exclusion robust under the concurrent `load()`/`loadCategories()` calls\n   (TASK-3). The notebook overview at `src/routes/notes/+page.svelte` reads the snapshot\n   fields `notes.favoriteNotes`/`notes.newestNotes`/`notes.lastUpdatedNotes`, which are\n   populated by `load()` before `journalCategory` may be resolved. Either derive the\n   overview from the live getters or re-snapshot those fields at the end of\n   `loadCategories()`. A store test that runs `load()` and `loadCategories()`\n   concurrently (or asserts the fields are filtered once `journalCategory` is set) would\n   lock this down.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":95,"totalLines":95,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/exist_notebook-journal/verdict.md","time":{"start":1791639638924,"end":1791639639316}},"id":"prt_1260b5366001WfjJUji6wdWcef","sessionID":"ses_ed9f4e243ffefIDWX0046IKymc","messageID":"msg_1260b4c150013jXihhUlBWMcw3"}}
